[
  {
    "lesson_id": "061",
    "trigger_word": "recommend",
    "trigger_card_number": 408,
    "title": "LECCIÓN 61: ESSENTIAL THAT HE BE",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Tras unos pocos verbos y adjetivos de",
          "exigencia, el inglés deja el verbo",
          "DESNUDO: sin -s, sin does, sin pasado.",
          "",
          "\"We recommend that he be told at once.\"",
          "no \"that he is told.\"",
          "\"They insisted that she stay.\"",
          "\"It is essential that the door remain",
          "shut.\""
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Los disparadores son pocos:",
          "recommend, insist, demand, propose,",
          "suggest, request — y",
          "vital, essential, important, crucial.",
          "",
          "La forma desnuda no cambia con he, she",
          "o it, y su negación no lleva do:",
          "\"We ask that he not be disturbed.\"",
          "",
          "El inglés británico suele preferir",
          "should: \"We recommend that he should",
          "be told.\" Ambas formas son correctas.",
          "",
          "El español usa aquí el subjuntivo ('que",
          "se le avise'). Al inglés solo le queda",
          "este rincón del suyo."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "062",
    "trigger_word": "leak",
    "trigger_card_number": 467,
    "title": "LECCIÓN 62: IT IS SAID THAT",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Cuando la fuente no importa, o no se",
          "quiere nombrar, el inglés informa a",
          "distancia.",
          "",
          "it + be + said/believed/reported + that:",
          "\"It is said that the leak came from",
          "inside.\"",
          "\"It was believed that nobody survived.\""
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "La misma idea puede colgar del sujeto:",
          "sujeto + be + thought + to + verbo.",
          "\"He is thought to be abroad.\"",
          "= Se cree que está en el extranjero.",
          "\"She is believed to have left already.\"",
          "",
          "Fíjate en los tiempos: to be = ahora;",
          "to have left = antes del informe.",
          "",
          "Es el registro de la prensa, la ciencia",
          "y la administración: afirma sin",
          "comprometer a nadie.",
          "",
          "El español recurre al 'se dice' o al",
          "impersonal; el inglés usa la pasiva y",
          "un it vacío."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "063",
    "trigger_word": "contrary",
    "trigger_card_number": 537,
    "title": "LECCIÓN 63: ¿CUÁNTO DE SEGURO?",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "El inglés cuidadoso gradúa lo que",
          "afirma en vez de proclamarlo.",
          "",
          "seem / appear to = eso parece.",
          "\"The figures appear to be wrong.\"",
          "tend to = suele, no siempre.",
          "\"Prices tend to rise in spring.\"",
          "be likely to = probablemente.",
          "\"He is likely to refuse.\""
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Hay palabras sueltas que hacen lo mismo:",
          "apparently = según parece.",
          "presumably = supongo que sí.",
          "arguably = puede sostenerse que.",
          "",
          "Y para dar la vuelta a una afirmación:",
          "on the contrary = al contrario.",
          "\"It did not help. On the contrary, it",
          "made things worse.\"",
          "",
          "Ojo: on the contrary CONTRADICE;",
          "in contrast solo compara.",
          "",
          "El español matiza con el subjuntivo y",
          "con adverbios; el inglés gasta palabras",
          "enteras en ello, y las espera."
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
]
